WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.700
Do we need a teacher to learn a language?

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.440
That's what I wanna talk about today.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:09.600
Uh, you know that I'm a person who
does, who enjoys, uh, self-study.

00:00:09.605 --> 00:00:12.030
I'm a self-motivated language learner.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:14.700
What do I think of the role of a teacher?

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:19.500
Well, I guess the quick answer
is do we need a teacher?

00:00:19.995 --> 00:00:25.725
The word "need" is strong,
but if the question were can

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:27.405
we benefit from a teacher?

00:00:27.465 --> 00:00:28.965
To me the answer is yes.

00:00:29.085 --> 00:00:32.055
And I'm gonna tell you when we
need the teacher or when the

00:00:32.055 --> 00:00:33.435
teacher can most benefit us.

00:00:34.035 --> 00:00:38.665
Uh, but there are polyglots like the
famous Hungarian polyglot, uh, Lomb

00:00:38.685 --> 00:00:41.055
Kato, who essentially learned on her own.

00:00:41.355 --> 00:00:44.385
There are a lot of very successful
polyglots who learn through reading,

00:00:44.385 --> 00:00:48.525
through listening, and who don't
require the services of a teacher.

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:53.670
Most people who think of learning a
language, think of finding a teacher.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.830
Uh, most people in the world, not the
sort of very active, self-motivated

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:02.310
polyglots, but most people who have
sort of a casual interest in learning

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:07.490
Spanish or Chinese, they think they have
to go to a classroom or find a teacher.

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:12.140
So upfront, I will say
you don't need a teacher.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:15.140
Like you can learn a
language without a teacher.

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:19.670
However, the teacher is very useful,
and there are two sort of situations:

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:24.380
one is the motivated learner and the
other is the unmotivated learner.

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:29.300
So when I was in my teens, I was
an unmotivated learner of French.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:35.160
At school, I had a teacher, a professor
at McGill University, who triggered my

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:39.150
interest in French and which subsequently
became an interest in other languages.

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:42.390
And he taught a course
in French civilization.

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:47.160
And the textbook was great and the way he
made it interesting, and he was a little

00:01:47.165 --> 00:01:52.170
bit sarcastic, which we all enjoyed, and
he was just a very stimulating teacher.

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:57.390
So for the unmotivated learner,
a teacher can be the trigger.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.210
A teacher can be the
person who gets you going.

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:06.360
So in that situation, if you're not
motivated, you need a teacher unless

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:07.470
you have some other motivation.

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:11.640
Might be, uh, you know, a spouse or a
girlfriend or a boyfriend or something

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:15.990
else, but something has to trigger that
interest and very often it's a teacher.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.720
Teacher can trigger an
interest, a teacher...

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:23.280
you wanna then learn the language to show
the teacher, teacher becomes a source of

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:29.280
feedback, a source of encouragement, uh,
somebody that you want to show that you

00:02:29.285 --> 00:02:31.020
are, you know, learning the language.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:33.750
So that's for the unmotivated learner.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:37.710
For the motivated learner,
I think a teacher can still

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:38.760
be of tremendous benefit.

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:44.220
However, the role of the teacher
is not to explain the language.

00:02:45.614 --> 00:02:48.704
The teacher's not necessarily the
source of the language because

00:02:48.945 --> 00:02:53.505
there is an abundance of sources
of language, especially today.

00:02:54.315 --> 00:02:58.635
Uh, on the internet, wherever
podcasts, eBooks, audiobooks,

00:02:58.965 --> 00:03:03.045
there's language everywhere and
there's an abundance of explanation.

00:03:03.285 --> 00:03:04.605
You can Google anything you want.

00:03:04.605 --> 00:03:10.065
Subjunctive in French or, you know, cases
in Slavic languages or whatever you want.

00:03:10.485 --> 00:03:15.435
So the teacher doesn't have to be the
source of knowledge about the language.

00:03:15.435 --> 00:03:17.175
Doesn't have to be an explainer.

00:03:17.415 --> 00:03:21.885
In fact, explanations are are rel...

00:03:21.975 --> 00:03:23.774
are not that tremendously useful.

00:03:24.105 --> 00:03:28.454
If you haven't had enough exposure to the
language, the explanation kind of passes.

00:03:28.454 --> 00:03:33.825
You buy a lot of the sort of how the
language works, you're gonna get used

00:03:33.825 --> 00:03:35.834
to it and figure it out on your own.

00:03:36.045 --> 00:03:38.475
It is sometimes useful
to have that explained.

00:03:38.804 --> 00:03:43.394
So here's where I think the teacher
is most useful for the motivated

00:03:43.394 --> 00:03:46.274
learner and that is at a later stage.

00:03:46.515 --> 00:03:52.905
Because initially the motivated learner
can find content at his or her level,

00:03:53.765 --> 00:03:56.865
uh, which could be the many stories at
LingQ, which as you know, I push them

00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:58.275
because there's a lot of repetition.

00:03:58.455 --> 00:04:03.285
But there's, there's Duolingo, there's,
uh, you know, uh, Pimsler, there's all

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:08.235
kinds of different systems that offer
you, uh, content at your level, which you

00:04:08.235 --> 00:04:13.125
can listen to, and you can read, and you
can get, you know, your feet wet in the

00:04:13.125 --> 00:04:18.464
language and you don't need a teacher to
explain the language to you at that time.

00:04:18.584 --> 00:04:22.875
I think the teacher is least,
if you're motivated, is least

00:04:22.875 --> 00:04:25.365
necessary in the early stages.

00:04:25.485 --> 00:04:28.665
In the early stages, you actually
have to get in there and start

00:04:28.665 --> 00:04:30.405
experiencing the language.

00:04:30.675 --> 00:04:35.784
However, as you progress in the language,
and I have had this experience, as

00:04:35.784 --> 00:04:39.805
you have some sense of the language,
you've, you've got these words building

00:04:39.805 --> 00:04:42.085
up in your mind, vocabulary ,phrases.

00:04:42.085 --> 00:04:44.425
You're listening to it, you're
understanding it better and better.

00:04:44.605 --> 00:04:45.745
Now you wanna speak.

00:04:46.665 --> 00:04:50.805
And when you wanna speak, you
need a teacher or a tutor or

00:04:50.835 --> 00:04:52.035
someone to speak with you.

00:04:52.455 --> 00:04:55.155
But when you start speaking in the
language, you're not very good.

00:04:55.515 --> 00:05:00.375
So anyone that speaks with you
has to be tolerant, has to help

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:02.325
you build up your speaking skills.

00:05:02.475 --> 00:05:06.405
You can't just approach, I mean you
can, but I find it less useful to,

00:05:06.945 --> 00:05:10.215
to deal with sort of random people
'cause then you repeat the same few

00:05:10.215 --> 00:05:11.535
words that you have all the time.

00:05:11.775 --> 00:05:17.130
You need a teacher who is gonna help take
you past, you know what you're comfortable

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:22.679
using and push you sort of beyond your
comfort zone, get you to learn more words.

00:05:22.799 --> 00:05:25.469
You are gonna hear more
words from that teacher.

00:05:26.115 --> 00:05:29.745
Hopefully the teacher doesn't spend
too much time explaining things to

00:05:29.745 --> 00:05:34.275
you or telling you that today we're
gonna teach you the colors or, you

00:05:34.275 --> 00:05:37.875
know, the parts of the body that,
that the teacher is responsive

00:05:37.875 --> 00:05:39.735
to your interests and your needs.

00:05:40.034 --> 00:05:44.625
And, and I've had this experience with
teachers where I just, they just lead

00:05:44.625 --> 00:05:46.665
me along and I speak more and more.

00:05:47.055 --> 00:05:50.205
And of course at LingQ the teacher
sends me a report with all the

00:05:50.505 --> 00:05:53.685
words and phrases that I had trouble
using, and I go over those and.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:58.770
Uh, gradually, gradually, gradually,
my ability to speak improves.

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:03.780
So at that stage, which I would call
sort of, I, I, if we go back to the

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:08.680
European Framework of Reference, where
you got A1 and 2, B1 and 2, C1, and 2.

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:10.050
So A1is beginner.

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:13.740
I think at the beginner level, you really
don't need a teacher if you're motivated.

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:16.230
If you're not motivated, as I
said, that's a different story.

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:21.750
Once you reach the B level, you are
now ready to start engaging with a

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:24.960
guided speaking partner by def...

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:29.640
by definition in my mind, a teacher, you
may pay that person or you might have a

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:35.190
language exchange with that person, or
that person for some reason or other is,

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:40.830
uh, willing to patiently work with you to
help you along in your speaking ability.

00:06:41.429 --> 00:06:43.710
And, uh, I call that person a teacher.

00:06:44.115 --> 00:06:48.195
Amateur teacher, paid teacher,
freebie teacher, it doesn't matter.

00:06:48.285 --> 00:06:50.025
You need the teacher at that point.

00:06:50.265 --> 00:06:54.855
And the more you speak at that sort of
intermediate level, the faster you're

00:06:54.855 --> 00:06:56.985
gonna improve your speaking ability.

00:06:57.105 --> 00:07:00.165
But you still have to continue
with your input activities.

00:07:00.285 --> 00:07:06.735
So the conclusion is we don't need a
teacher, but it's great to have a teacher.

00:07:06.735 --> 00:07:08.385
I've had some great teachers.

00:07:08.685 --> 00:07:13.465
I mentioned the teacher who, you know,
started me off in my interest in French,

00:07:13.465 --> 00:07:15.025
and then therefore in other languages.

00:07:15.355 --> 00:07:20.275
I've had teachers who guide me, who find
me fascinating content of interest to

00:07:20.275 --> 00:07:24.565
me in Ukrainian, in Persian, in Polish.

00:07:25.015 --> 00:07:31.335
Uh, so the teacher can have a, a
tremendous role uh, in, in being your

00:07:31.335 --> 00:07:35.414
language learning support and inspiration.

00:07:36.075 --> 00:07:42.675
Uh, and I think the benefits are greater
the more we progress in the language, at

00:07:42.675 --> 00:07:45.645
least through that sort of B1 to B2 stage.

00:07:45.794 --> 00:07:49.125
Once you're past B2, once
again, you're on your own.

00:07:49.365 --> 00:07:50.625
So there you have it.

00:07:50.745 --> 00:07:55.395
My view on whether we need a teacher
and how the teacher can most help us.

00:07:56.235 --> 00:07:56.775
Thank you.

00:07:56.925 --> 00:07:57.224
Bye.

